cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CASTELLAN or its eval sets, please cite it as below."
title: "CASTELLAN: residual-stream probes for secrets and PII in LLM and agent traffic, measured across an obfuscation ladder"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dayal
    given-names: Apoorv
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Apoorv13/castellan"
url: "https://github.com/Apoorv13/castellan"
keywords:
  - secret detection
  - PII detection
  - interpretability
  - linear probes
  - residual stream
  - LLM security
  - obfuscation
abstract: >-
  CASTELLAN detects secrets and PII in LLM and agent traffic by reading a
  language model's residual-stream activations with small trained probes. It
  returns character spans, class labels and calibrated scores. The project
  measures how probe recall holds up as a secret is disguised past regex
  scanners (split, encoded, homoglyphs, spelled out, reassembled across turns),
  compares it with Gitleaks and Presidio, and relates it to whether the model
  can read the disguised secret, across Qwen3 0.6B to 8B. Code is Apache-2.0;
  the synthetic eval sets are CC-BY-4.0.
